# .gitignore — jvlevinson/jvlevinson (GitHub profile repository)
#
# SCOPE: artifacts a clone of THIS repo can produce. OS cruft (.DS_Store,
# Thumbs.db, desktop.ini, *~) is deliberately ABSENT — that belongs in the
# per-user global excludes file:
#   git config --global core.excludesFile ~/.config/git/ignore
#
# Verify a rule with:  git status --porcelain --ignored
# NOT with `git check-ignore` alone — it exits 0 on a NEGATED match too, so
# `check-ignore .env.example` succeeds even though the file is tracked.


# --- Editor local history ----------------------------------------------------
# VS Code "Local History" extension. Unanchored: it can write at any depth.
# Kept in-repo rather than global so the rule survives fresh clones and CI.
.history/


# --- Personal scratch space --------------------------------------------------
# Work-in-progress that must never render on a public profile page.
# Anchored: only the repo-root directory, never a nested `experimental/`.
/experimental/


# --- Local tooling deployed into this repo -----------------------------------
# Timestamp scripts and their run log. Machine-local; must not reach the
# public profile. Anchored so a future docs/01-project/reports/ is never
# silently swallowed — unanchored `reports/` matches at ANY depth.
/.scripts/
/reports/


# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# A guard, not a control: this repo reads no env vars, and GitHub secret
# scanning + push protection are the mechanisms that would actually fire.
# Two lines against an asymmetric downside on a public repo.
#
# This negation is safe because `.env.*` matches FILES. Negation can NEVER
# rescue a file whose parent directory is excluded — git does not descend into
# excluded directories. There are no directory negations in this file.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example


# --- AI coding-agent local artifacts -----------------------------------------
# Histories, caches and logs only. Agent INSTRUCTION files stay TRACKED on
# purpose — CLAUDE.md is shared via source control. Do NOT blanket-ignore
# `.claude/`.
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/*.local.json
.claude/**/*.log


# --- Deliberately NOT ignored — do not add rules matching these ---------------
# The metrics workflow commits assets/github-metrics.svg back to main
# (output_action: commit, committer_branch: main). Any `*.svg`, `assets/`, or
# pasted-in Images.gitignore rule would break that round-trip and make
# `git status` lie about the generated file.
#
# If you add further images to the profile, host them HERE rather than on an
# external CDN — the README's banner already 403s for exactly that reason.
#
#   README.md                  <- the profile page itself
#   .github/workflows/         <- metrics.yml
#   assets/github-metrics.svg  <- generated; never hand-edit
#   .gitignore
#   CLAUDE.md                  <- repo-scoped operating rules, no host details
#   docs/                      <- documentation scaffold
